  "sids/GAMES/S-Z/World_Cup.sid": "COMMENT: The game chooses one of three tunes to play at random for the in-game\n         music, based on the value of the C64's timer, and chooses again at the\n         end of play to make the in-game soundtrack. Subtune #1 in this rip\n         replicates this so will play a random choice of the tunes. Subtunes #2\n         to #4 have been added to play each tune individually.\n(#1)\nCOMMENT: Plays tune #2, #3 and #4 in random order.\n(#2)\n  TITLE: Blue Is The Colour\n ARTIST: Daniel Boone & Rod McQueen\nCOMMENT: Performed by Chelsea FC for their 1972 League Cup final single, and\n         an anthem played at the club since then.\n(#3)\n  TITLE: Nice One Cyril\n ARTIST: Harold Spiro & Helen Clarke (The Cockerel Chorus)\nCOMMENT: Made for Tottenham Hotspur FC for their 1973 League Cup final single,\n         and sung on the terrces by fans since then.\n(#4)\n  TITLE: I'm Forever Blowing Bubbles\n ARTIST: John Kelette\nCOMMENT: Adopted by West Ham United FC during the 1940s as a popular football\n         chant, and has been used by their fans since then. The club also\n         re-recorded the song for their 1975 FA Cup final single.",
  "sids/GAMES/S-Z/World_Games.sid": "COMMENT: The game also uses /GAMES/S-Z/Summer_Games.sid, Tunes #2-#21\n(#3)\n  TITLE: Ach, du lieber Augustin\n ARTIST: Traditional\nCOMMENT: Austrian folk song.\n(#6)\n  TITLE: The Lumberjack Song\n ARTIST: Terry Jones, Michael Palin & Fred Tomlinson\nCOMMENT: Text by Terry Jones & Michael Palin.\n(#8)\n  TITLE: Piobaireachd of Donald Dhu\n ARTIST: Scottish Traditional\nCOMMENT: \"Piobaireachd\" is pronounced approximately \"pee-brock\".\n(#9)\n  TITLE: Highland Laddie\n ARTIST: Scottish Traditional",
