  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Acceleration-mix.sid": "  TITLE: Owner of a Lonely Heart [from 90125] (0:00-0:55)\n ARTIST: Yes\n  TITLE: Mammagamma (0:57-1:16)\n ARTIST: Alan Parsons Project\n  TITLE: Hawkeye [from Vulture Culture] (1:24-1:55)\n ARTIST: Alan Parsons Project",
  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Afterburner.sid": "(#1)\n  TITLE: After Burner [from the arcade game After Burner II]\n ARTIST: Hiroshi Kawaguchi (Hiro/SEGA Sound Team)\nCOMMENT: Freestyle cover based on the arcade original.\n(#2)\n  TITLE: Super Stripe [from the arcade game After Burner II]\n ARTIST: Hiroshi Kawaguchi (Hiro/SEGA Sound Team)\nCOMMENT: A somewhat loose cover, especially later in the tune.",
  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Alloyrun.sid": "(#1)\n   NAME: Title tune\n(#2)\n   NAME: High-score\n(#3)\n   NAME: Get-ready",
  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Arpverhaal.sid": "COMMENT: Early version of /MUSICIANS/T/Tel_Jeroen/2400_AD.sid, Tune #1.",
  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Aspar_Grand_Prix_Master.sid": "COMMENT: Also used in level 2 of the game \"After the War\", (C) 1989 Dinamic.",
  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Bad_Blood.sid": "(#2)\n  TITLE: Vall�t\n ARTIST: <?>\nCOMMENT: The tune might be inspired by this piece.\n         Q: Is this a cover?\n         JT: NO! Worldshocking huh? I could actually compose music in the\n         classical traditional sence :) It's all COMPOSED by me. More people\n         seemed to be wondering if I *really composed Bad Blood*. The answer is\n         yes with a capital Y.\n         Charles Deenen said it was the \"best music I made on C64\" when I\n         finished it. (I do NOT agree ofcourse, although I must say it's the\n         best \"filmscore\" soundtrack I've done for a game on the C64. I\n         actually got some kind of filmscript for it, that's why I could be\n         very specific when composing themes for characters and events in the\n         game.",
  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Bantam.sid": "COMMENT: From about 0:50, the melody resembles",
  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Beginning.sid": "  TITLE: Scroll It Up!\n ARTIST: Jeroen Tel\nCOMMENT: Covers /MUSICIANS/T/Tel_Jeroen/Scroll_It_Up.sid",
