  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Children_Songs.sid": "(#1)\nCOMMENT: \"These are all melodies I just knew from hearing around, you know, I\n         added some titles of the original works. |:) \" (JT)\n  TITLE: Kabouter Spillebeen (0:15-0:19)\n ARTIST: <?>\n  TITLE: Yankee Doodle (0:23-0:30)\n ARTIST: Traditional, Dr. Richard Schuckburgh (lyrics)\n  TITLE: Fr�re Jacques (0:53-1:01)\n ARTIST: Traditional\nCOMMENT: French folk song.\n  TITLE: Dixie Land (1:24-1:31)\n ARTIST: Daniel Emmett\n  TITLE: Kabouter Spillebeen (1:55-2:02)\n ARTIST: <?>\n  TITLE: London Bridge is Falling Down (2:10-2:18)\n ARTIST: Traditional children's song",
  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Dan_Dare_3.sid": "(#1)\nCOMMENT: The author of S.O.A.P.'s hit \"This Is How We Party\", said in an\n         interview that he was inspired by the chords between 0:23 and 0:31.",
  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Daring_Dots.sid": "COMMENT: \"It's a simple TEST-tune to check the 'digi-player'.\" (JT)",
  "sids/Tel_Jeroen/Dying_High.sid": "(#2)\n  TITLE: Jeroen\n ARTIST: Jeroen Tel",
